Z||000002||SKIDMARK||11-08-2001||01:49 AM||||Both of my Fieros had the same problem. It seems that when the bearings/bushings wear out int the fan motor it wobbles just enough to hit the plastic fan shroud. The fan motor is about $22 at AutoZone. That cured my noisy fans.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-08-2001||11:33 PM||||Could be the motor or a warped/unbalanced/cracked fan. After all these years allot of plastic fans aren't true anymore, especially the rim around the outside of the blades.<P>Also, take the fan off and carefully check each blade and the rim. look them over for cracks, chips, and any crap, like undercoating, that may be stuck there. Even a little weight change on one blade will increase vibration tremendously. Pull on things and see if any cracks open. They can be hard to see. Just don't pull so hard you make a crack... (If it cracks easily it was soon to break. The fans are pretty tough.)<P>The motor is pretty easy to fix. The fan blades are easy if you can find a good set close to the same size. It can be a little smaller and/or have more blades. You'll likely have to dig around the scrap yards for blades...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
